<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,349.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,349.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,349 today from 1,343 on July 4, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1423    12.917	  1409    12.793</p>
<p>   1a   1334 10100.000	  1330 10071.000</p>
<p>   2    1661    23.725	  1650    23.571</p>
<p>   2a   1584 12992.000	  1571 12886.000</p>
<p>   3    1470    13.558	  1458    13.450</p>
<p>   3a   1264  9975.000	  1261  9950.000</p>
<p>   6    1289    13.293	  1288    13.281</p>
